# 0018 — bound inline-image payloads (T4.4 hardening)
#
# WHY: OSC 1337 File=;inline=1 is rendered BY THE VENDOR (Terminal.swift osciTerm2 ->
# TerminalView.createImage), and createImage is `public` in an extension, not `open`, so
# the app cannot guard it. Upstream v1.15.0 had no bound anywhere on that path:
#   (a) EscapeSequenceParser accumulated an OSC without limit (unterminated payload =
#       unbounded memory). Now capped at 65 MiB, upstream main's own number and name
#       (_oscLimitExceeded); an over-limit OSC is consumed to its terminator and dropped,
#       so the parser stays in sync and the next sequence works.
#   (b) osciTerm2 base64-decoded any size. Now rejects > 32 MiB encoded BEFORE decode.
#   (c) createImage ran NSImage(data:) on anything, incl. PDF/EPS and decompression
#       bombs. Now reads type + pixel size from the ImageIO header first: raster
#       allowlist (png/jpeg/gif/tiff/bmp/heic/webp) and max side 8192 px.
#   (d) createImageFromBitmap (sixel) refuses sides > 8192 or a short buffer.
# Every rejection is a silent drop: no crash, no partial insert, no log.
# Gate: app/Scripts/check-image-decode.sh (falsified by removing each guard).
